  "question": {
    "text": "Assuming that the human pupil has a radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25&#160;</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> and a comfortable viewing distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The minimum separation between two point objects that the human eye can resolve for the light of wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>&nbsp;is",
